  "gait": "The gait stays up for 12.0 s and moves 537 mm forward (48.8 mm/s). The feet leave the floor in turn: the highest a whole sole comes off the floor is 6.18 mm, and both feet stay loaded 41 percent of the time. In the fuller servo model of the motion study the same gait walks at 41.9 mm/s, makes 97 percent of its steps with a sole clear of the floor, peaks at 0.658 of the torque limit and stayed up in 30 of 30 perturbed runs.",
